captures the "knee" of the aggregate habitat-count vs. \code{minPts} curve at the derived \code{eps}.
This curve marks the physical transition from culling accidental noise points to eroding
genuine habitat clusters.

Its operational meaning is temporal: \verb{minPts * sampling_interval = minimum residence duration}.
Alternatively, users can explicitly supply \code{min_residence} (in days) to enforce a direct
behavioral floor, which is converted to fix counts using the median sampling interval.
}

